//
// Normative rule hstatus_hu_op (src/priv/hypervisor.adoc):
//   Field HU (Hypervisor in U-mode) controls whether the virtual-machine load/store instructions,
//     HLV, HLVX, and HSV, can be used also in U-mode. When HU=1, these instructions can be executed
//     in U-mode the same as in HS-mode. When HU=0, all hypervisor instructions cause an illegal-
//     instruction exception in U-mode.
//
// Context:
//   "The same as in HS-mode" includes the data: with vsatp and hgatp Bare, a U-mode HLV returns
//     what an HS-mode HLV returns, and a U-mode HSV writes memory. HU never enables HFENCE or
//     HINVAL in U-mode (hfence-vvma_hfence-gvma_exceptions).
//
